## Identity guard (assertOwnIdentityOnly) behavior — as observed, not edited
Read skills/_shared/lib/identity-guard.mjs before running: `assertOwnIdentityOnly(line,
opts)` checks TWO things only — (1) no user-PII env var pattern present in the process env
(USER_*, GOOGLE_LOGIN, COMPOSIO, GCAL, GMAIL, TELEGRAM, USER_PHONE/CONTACT), and (2) the
ledger line's `source` field is on ALLOWED_EARN_SOURCES (which includes "hl-trade",
"hl"). It does NOT compare the `wallet` field against any "own wallet" allowlist or
per-instance identity file anywhere in this module or in record.mjs.

Consequence, observed directly: across all 71 real record.mjs subprocess invocations in
pass1 (payload wallet = 0xa3cdd4ec6b94f01826aaf90a6d5538a2aa8c4c21, the OLD/rotated,
non-current-instance wallet), every single one returned exit code 0 with stdout
"PROFITABLE" and NO "P1-GUARD HALT" message on stderr. A standalone probe run directly
against record.mjs (same wallet, throwaway ledger path, fill_tid=999999, cleaned up
immediately after) reproduced this: exit=0, stdout "PROFITABLE", stderr "recorded
net=0.009 tx=- status=-", no HALT line.

This means: for THIS feature (hl-realized-pnl), no wallet-address-based identity HALT
exists in the current code — assertOwnIdentityOnly gates only on env-PII and the
`source` string, both of which this run legitimately satisfies (source="hl-trade" is
correctly allowlisted; no user-PII env vars were present in this shell). The runbook's
contingency ("if the identity guard HALTs for the non-own wallet, that IS the evidence;
otherwise use the record_line_fn injectable seam") did not need to be invoked because no
HALT occurred at all — the real record_line path ran to completion cleanly. This is
reported as observed behavior only; no code was changed and no judgment is offered here
about whether a wallet-level check SHOULD exist (out of scope for this execution task).

